{
  "title": "FOAM coupled ocean-atmosphere runs every 20 Myr, 540-0 Ma: surface currents for the past maps (wwolf P02 step 3)",
  "retrieved": "2026-09-22",
  "record": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5780097",
  "license": "CC BY 4.0 (Zenodo record metadata)",
  "cite": "Pohl, A., Ridgwell, A., Stockey, R. G., Thomazo, C., Keane, A., Vennin, E. & Scotese, C. R. (2022). Continental configuration controls ocean oxygenation during the Phanerozoic. Nature, 608, 523-527. doi:10.1038/s41586-022-05018-z. Data: Pohl, A., Phanerozoic global climatic fields simulated using the FOAM ocean-atmosphere general circulation model, Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.5780097.",
  "note": "The ocean component of each run: monthly U, V in m/s on 24 levels from -5300 m up to -10 m of a 128x128 grid (2.8 x 1.4 degrees). All runs share CO2 2240 ppm, a 1368 W/m2 Sun, a circular orbit at minimum obliquity and rocky-desert land; only the Scotese & Wright (2018) geography changes, so the currents show what the continents do, not each period's climate. The paper's data availability statement points to this record (concept doi:10.5281/zenodo.5780096). scripts/build_past_currents.py takes the top level's annual mean of the slice nearest each PaleoDEM stop.",
